# Security

See also `SECURITY.md` at repo root.

## Network & auth

- Default bind: `127.0.0.1`
- LAN (`0.0.0.0`) only with explicit activation + pairing codes
- Gateway bearer tokens for authenticated access
- Skills have no automatic system rights — Permission Policy + audit logs for sensitive ops

## Electron

- `contextIsolation: true`, `nodeIntegration: false`, `sandbox: true`
- Validate all IPC with Zod from `@involvex/ctrl-s`
- CSP; block navigation and unsolicited `window.open`

## Secrets & data

- Never store secrets in `app.db`
- Prefer OS stores: Electron `safeStorage`, Android Keystore
- Never commit tokens/keys; keep secrets out of argv/logs
- Document env vars (e.g. `CTRL_TOKEN`, `CTRL_HOST`, `CTRL_PORT`, embeddings keys) without committing values

## Input

- Validate all external inputs at boundaries with `@involvex/ctrl-s` Zod schemas
- Parameterized SQL only via the gateway DB layer (`ctrl-z`)
- Do not expose internal stack traces to clients

## Checklist (before shipping network-facing changes)

- [ ] Loopback default preserved or LAN pairing documented
- [ ] Auth / pairing paths covered
- [ ] IPC and HTTP bodies Zod-validated
- [ ] No secrets in DB, logs, or git
- [ ] Lockfile present (`bun.lock`); deps reviewed for advisories
